---
description: Split a procedure into phases; leave opcode switches and pixel loops whole
globs: packages/engine/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Functions

A function that runs a sequence of phases is several functions. The function that owns the order (`frame`, `enter`, `tick`) keeps the early returns and the `await` order. A phase is one call.

An opcode `switch` stays one `switch`. `SceneHost.run` and `Interpreter.step` are dispatch, not a hidden second algorithm. Cases that share a body stay adjacent and call one function. `noFallthroughCasesInSwitch` is on.

A loop over pixels or samples stays nested. That depth is the algorithm (`boxScale`, `darken`, `softenEdges`, `drawFrame`).

A nest that only skips input, or that hides a second decision, becomes a named function. The outer function stays the search or the scan (`Search.rec`, `resolveClick`, `turningTick`).

A boolean gate is a local name (`walking`, `ignoreClick`). It is not a new function.

A file under the line limit stays one file, unless a shared helper is leaving it.

```ts
// Wrong: one function per opcode.
case WORDS.TALK:
  return runTalk(host);

// Right: the switch stays. A phase of frame is a call, in the same order.
if (hotspotFrame.call(this, input) === "verb") return;
pendingFrame.call(this);
```
